{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/assets/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{7}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{7}Mr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-0+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31M}{35}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dc536cfdbcf6cc9baa7cf539affc2cc1dcbbfaf89a5fab64bce73dfc01eaf1cc"} {"question" "q-163586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{15}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{21}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=3x,$ $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{5}+9{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}[2{x}^{6}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}\\cdot (128-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dc536cfdbcf6cc9baa7cf539affc2cc1dcbbfaf89a5fab64bce73dfc01eaf1cc"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{6}x{y}^{6}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{20}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dc536cfdbcf6cc9baa7cf539affc2cc1dcbbfaf89a5fab64bce73dfc01eaf1cc"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{7}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{20}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 6.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{y}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{6},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =4M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dc536cfdbcf6cc9baa7cf539affc2cc1dcbbfaf89a5fab64bce73dfc01eaf1cc"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dc536cfdbcf6cc9baa7cf539affc2cc1dcbbfaf89a5fab64bce73dfc01eaf1cc"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"} {"question" "q-163658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe6c89968df0cdbde12a9c2828855969758e83cb055ef84163661785bf1a6905"}] "usage" {"q-163586" []} "basis" 2865 "retractions" [[17592186198590 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4174/Source/Images/q-163586.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles $x^{2} + y^{2} = 1$, $x^{2} + y^{2} = 4$, and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $λ(x, y) = \\frac{3}{7}My$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186194442 17592186194443 17592186194444 17592186194445 17592186194446] "immutable_fields" [[17592186194441 :answer-field/correct] [17592186194441 :answer-field/id] [17592186194441 :answer-field/key] [17592186194441 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
